SCENE — the same wide suburban boulevard, seen dead-on, but now resolved into something clean and orderly: a straight row of identical low pale plinths running horizontally across the frame, each carrying one ordinary grey car, each lit evenly from above by a simple slim pale gantry. Above each car, mounted on its gantry, is a completely blank rectangular panel — no lettering, no digits, no markings of any kind on any panel. The plinths are evenly spaced and perfectly aligned, receding to left and right. The ground between them is clean pale tarmac. Palm trees and low pale apartment blocks sit far behind. Every parked car is an ordinary lifeless grey vehicle with no face. No people.

The camera is level and square-on; the row of plinths runs straight and horizontal across the frame.

THE GREEN CAR IS SEEN FROM BEHIND AND SLIGHTLY TO ONE SIDE — a rear three-quarter view. Its nose points AWAY from the camera and to the RIGHT, down the row. We see its plain back and its boot lid, with NO face on it, and we see its right flank. It is driving away from us along the row, to the right. It faces this same way in both frames and never turns round.
@@A@@ It is at the LEFT of centre, part-way along the row.
@@B@@ It has driven further along and is now at the RIGHT of centre, still pointing away from the camera and to the right, still driving in the same direction. The row of plinths, gantries and grey cars is completely unchanged.
